  <section class="section-compact animals-response-band" aria-labelledby="animals-response-title">
    <div class="shell animals-response-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Suspected poisoning?</p>
        <h2 id="animals-response-title">Call a vet or wildlife rehabilitator now.</h2>
        <p>For a pet, contact your nearest veterinarian. For a wild animal or bird of prey, contact a licensed wildlife rehabilitator or your nearest veterinarian for advice. Do not wait for symptoms to become severe, and do not attempt treatment yourself.</p>
        <p>If you know which product may be involved, keep its packaging or take a photograph only if you can do so safely. The product identity can help a veterinarian decide what care is needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="animals-response-links">
        <p class="eyebrow">Find the right help</p>
        <a href="/documents/wildlife-and-raptor-rehabilitation-centres-south-africa.pdf">Wildlife and raptor rehabilitation centres in South Africa <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="visually-hidden"> (PDF)</span></a>
